All right.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:18.420
Well, I thought about that question, and this is what I thought I need to improve on.

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:21.540
Algebra.

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:23.260
Algebra.

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:24.660
How could you miss that?

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:27.160
How did you overlook that?

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:28.260
I don't know.

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:29.580
We actually talked about that.

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:35.780
I have to say, also, one of the things that's so odd is that at most weddings you never see people have any kind of discord.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:36.820
Yeah.

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:49.680
My dream would have been that we were just failing miserably, which oddly enough happened, and that everybody thought we weren't going to be able to get married, and the last question was just a truly impossible question that we both had to get right in order to get married.

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:52.900
And there were some people who didn't think we were going to pull it off.

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:54.780
There were some people who thought we weren't going to make it.

00:10:55.400 --> 00:11:01.280
I find that, I mean, I've only seen the videotape of this, but I find it hard to believe that people would believe that.

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:07.900
Well, you know, I thought it was going to be hard to believe too, but I looked at people's faces and they were really, well, what are we going to do?

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:08.640
What are you going to do now?

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:10.880
Oh, they totally believed it.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:16.330
There are people who came up to me and they said, I didn't think you guys were going to make it and I thought it was just going to be a big party and nothing else.

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:17.620
Where are we at?

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:19.740
We're still at 20.

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:21.520
Holding at 20.

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:55.260
another unusual moment in your ceremony that is certainly not very traditional in a wedding is that you talk about the bathroom what did we I don't remember this what are you talking about who spends more time in the bathroom Carl Wendy Wendy I'd say that too Wendy what do you say absolutely Carl wait a minute If you saw his bathroom and you saw how much cleaner it is than mine, you'd know he spent more time in there at least cleaning.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:56.960
That's good, Carl.

